**1 [[R.Ost]] spawns after 90 seconds<sup>2,700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Don't waste any time here; clear the Squire Rels as fast as possible and instantly obliterate Gobble with [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cats]]. A single R.Ost on his own is trivial enough to hold back while you build up your wallet. Your best friends throughout this entire run are going to be [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Ironcat]], [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]], and [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]], who put a cork in the Traitless fiends. Traditional meatshielding is simply not an option, as it drains your cash insanely quickly and there are no enemies at all to replenish from. You will have to make do with [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] and [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]]/[[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] to hold him back alongside the other anti-Traitless crowd-controllers.

You will need all the cash you can get your grubby hands on to deal with the absolutely hellish combination of enemies that appear during the boss wave. Luckily, Oldhorn has negative synergy with Kappy, and completely prevents him from getting an attack off until he's dealt with. He will also prevent you from stacking anything up, so you have to kill him ASAP before R.Ost spawns. If you have [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]], use her, otherwise [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] are your best means to that end. You do need some lucky Fishman hits to get rid of the Gobbles right after Oldhorn bites the dust. Once it's just Kappy and R.Ost by their lonesome, your anti-Traitless cats + [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando Jr.]] will have an easy enough time keeping them at bay while you slowly kill the duo. Try not to run out of cash, though.

If you happen to own [[Filibuster Cat X (Special Cat)|Talented Metafilibuster]], he makes this whole stage a much easier ordeal as he matches up great into Kappy, Oldhorn, and R.Ost as well as outranging Gobble's omni. Pair him with anti-surge package units and he'll destroy this frustrating cast of enemies.

